{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Patel. I understand you came in from your transplant clinic today. Can you tell me how you’ve been feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, yes. I’ve been feeling really weak lately, and I just feel… dehydrated. My legs are a little swollen too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Your kidney function came up in clinic — your creatinine is up to 3.5, which is higher than your usual 2.5. That’s why we’re admitting you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s not good. It was already high before. Is this another kidney flare-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like acute on chronic kidney injury. Your blood count shows hemoconcentration — your hematocrit went from 26 to 32 — which suggests dehydration may be playing a big role."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been drinking much. I’ve been so tired. But I also have this terrible tremor — it’s making everything hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see you were on primidone for that, but it was stopped recently because it can interfere with your tacrolimus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. My levels went up — they said it was 6, which is high. But the shaking hasn’t improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor that. For now, we’re going to give you IV fluids to help your kidneys, and we’ll check your labs daily to see how you’re responding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And what about my urine infection? I saw something about Klebsiella."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your urine culture grew Klebsiella pneumoniae. It’s sensitive to most antibiotics, so we’ll start you on ceftriaxone to treat the infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve had UTIs before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, especially with your medical history. We’re treating it early to prevent it from worsening or spreading."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my eye surgery — it’s scheduled for this week. Will that still happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to go ahead with your cataract and glaucoma laser procedure. It’s important for your vision, and your team feels it’s safe once your kidney function stabilizes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been struggling to see clearly. But I’m nervous about anesthesia with everything going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2200-12-03 20:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The anesthesiologist will review your case. We’ll make sure your blood pressure and kidney function are stable first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2200-12-04 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are improving slightly. We’re continuing IV fluids and antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2200-12-04 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel a little less tired today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2200-12-04 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also adjusting your insulin — your blood sugars have been running high, so we added a bit more to your regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2200-12-04 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Diabetes never makes things easier. My eyes and kidneys both suffer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2200-12-04 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. That’s why we’re being careful with your fluids and sugars. You’re doing well so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2200-12-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to take you for your eye procedure — cataract removal and glaucoma laser on the left eye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2200-12-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. Will I notice a difference right away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2200-12-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Vision may be blurry at first, but over the next few days, you should see improvement. We’ll keep an eye patch on for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2200-12-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure went well. The surgeon replaced your lens and completed the laser treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2200-12-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My eye feels a little pressure, but not pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2200-12-04 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll give you drops to prevent infection and reduce inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2200-12-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest creatinine is down to 3.1 — that’s progress. Your urine output is good too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2200-12-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Does that mean I’m getting better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2200-12-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your kidneys are responding to hydration. We’ll keep the IV fluids going a bit longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2200-12-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the infection? Is the antibiotic working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2200-12-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The Klebsiella is sensitive to the antibiotic, and your white count is normalizing. We’ll finish a full course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2200-12-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound of your liver and blood vessels today — everything looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2200-12-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there any sign of clots or liver problems?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2200-12-06 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the hepatic vessels are patent, and there’s no sign of portal thrombosis. Your liver looks coarse, which is expected after transplant, but no new issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2200-12-06 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been worried about that since my last admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2200-12-07 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is now 2.8 — still improving. We’re going to start reducing IV fluids and encourage you to drink more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2200-12-07 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can do that. I’ve been sipping water all morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2200-12-07 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your tremor — we’re not changing meds now, but we’ll discuss options with neurology soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2200-12-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture is now clear — the antibiotic is working. We’ll switch to oral antibiotics soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2200-12-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it wouldn’t respond."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2200-12-08 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common bacteria, and we caught it early. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2200-12-09 15:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got the Doppler results back — your liver blood flow is normal. No clots, which is excellent news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2200-12-09 15:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s one less thing to worry about. How’s my kidney number today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2200-12-09 15:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Creatinine is 2.6 — very close to your baseline. We’re planning to stop IV fluids tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2200-12-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re off IV fluids now. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2200-12-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I have more energy, and my leg swelling is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2200-12-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your eye is healing well too — the ophthalmology team checked and said you’re healing as expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2200-12-11 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging antibiotics today — you’ll finish a week of oral cefdinir at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2200-12-11 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take them as directed. What about my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2200-12-11 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual — tacrolimus, insulin, and your other regulars. We’ll monitor your tremor at your next clinic visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2200-12-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is stable at 2.5 — that’s your baseline. We’re planning discharge soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2200-12-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2200-12-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One thing — you mentioned your caregiver has been living with you and it’s been stressful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2200-12-12 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she took over my room and made decisions for me. I asked her to move out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2200-12-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you spoke up. Your social worker will check in to make sure you’re safe and supported at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2200-12-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge is set for tomorrow. You’ll follow up with transplant, nephrology, and eye clinics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2200-12-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have all my appointments scheduled. I’ll keep drinking fluids and checking my sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2200-12-13 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And call if you feel weak, have fever, or notice changes in urination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2200-12-14 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last check — labs are stable, you’re eating well, and your eye is healing. Discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2200-12-14 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel like a new person."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2200-12-14 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Keep up with your follow-ups and stay hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2200-12-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick call to check in — how are you doing at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2200-12-15 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doing well. No fever, peeing fine, and my eye feels better every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2200-12-15 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Keep taking the antibiotics and monitor your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2200-12-16 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final update — your discharge papers are ready. You’re officially discharged as of today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2200-12-16 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll see you in clinic next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2200-12-16 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2200-12-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your anemia is still mild, so keep eating iron-rich foods and follow up with your blood counts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2200-12-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve been eating more meat and greens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2200-12-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. And remember, your history of liver cancer means we stay vigilant — regular scans are important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2200-12-16 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have my next ultrasound scheduled. I won’t miss it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2200-12-16 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your GERD — keep taking your omeprazole and avoid late meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2200-12-16 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been better about that. Less heartburn."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2200-12-16 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And for osteoporosis, keep taking your calcium and vitamin D."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2200-12-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your records. You’ve made excellent progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2200-12-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2200-12-16 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Stay on top of your health — you’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you have all your prescriptions and follow-up appointments?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, everything’s in my bag. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and see you in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final note: your discharge is official as of 16:40. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2200-12-16 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Stay healthy."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2200-12-03 20:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2200-12-16 16:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 72-year-old woman with a history of liver transplant for HCV cirrhosis, type 2 diabetes, and chronic kidney disease was admitted for acute on chronic kidney injury with creatinine elevated to 3.5 from a baseline of 2.5, in the setting of dehydration and hemoconcentration. She also had a urinary tract infection caused by Klebsiella pneumoniae, which was treated with intravenous then oral antibiotics. During admission, she underwent left eye cataract removal and ECP glaucoma laser procedure, which proceeded without complications. Her kidney function gradually improved with intravenous hydration, and creatinine stabilized at baseline by discharge. She reported resolution of weakness and dehydration symptoms. Social concerns regarding her caregiver were addressed before discharge. She was discharged home with follow-up arranged in transplant, nephrology, and ophthalmology clinics, and instructions to continue oral antibiotics, manage diabetes, and monitor kidney function.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Liver transplant status",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic chronic kidney disease",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with hyperglycemia",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with other diabetic ophthalmic complication",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Myasthenia gravis without (acute) exacerbation",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic cataract",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Unspecified glaucoma",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease with stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease",
      "Chronic kidney disease, stage 4 (severe)",
      "Essential tremor",
      "Encounter for follow-up examination after completed treatment for conditions other than malignant neoplasm",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of liver",
      "Age-related osteoporosis without current pathological fracture",
      "Personal history of peptic ulcer disease",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Other specified disorders of bone density and structure, unspecified site",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence",
      "Dehydration",
      "Klebsiella pneumoniae [K. pneumoniae] as the cause of diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Other specified abnormal findings of blood chemistry"
    ]
  }
}
